10-02 19:45:14.810  2511  2599 I AndroidLM: run=1 text[0]=The quantum-resistant digital signature algorithms standardized by NIST are ML-DSA (Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Algorithm) and SLH-DSA (Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Algorithm) [2]. ML-DSA is specified in FIPS 204 and is derived from CRYSTALS-Dilithium [2], [3]. SLH-DSA is specified in FIPS 205 and is derived from SPHINCS+ [2], [5]. Additionally, FALCON (FN-DSA) was selected by NIST as a quantum-resistant digital signature scheme [3].
10-02 19:45:14.810  2511  2599 I AndroidLM: 
10-02 19:45:14.810  2511  2599 I AndroidLM: These algorithms were selected through NIST's Post-Quantum Cryptography Standardization Process initiated in December 2016 to address the threat posed by large-scale quantum computers to classical public-key cryptosystems [3], [4]. ML-DSA and FALCON are based on structured lattices, while SLH-DSA is hash-based [3]. During the transition to post-quantum cryptography, these quantum-resistant algorithms may be deployed alongside quantum-vu
10-02 19:45:14.810  2511  2599 I AndroidLM: run=1 text[1]=lnerable algorithms to ensure interoperability [1].
